# SABOTAGE: A1 (ADR-047 §6 / RP-AG-8) gate sabotage — the agent loop's durable-interrupt
# semantics. The durable cancel re-check (`cancel_requested_at`, set by
# Samen.AI.Agent.cancel/2) moves from EVERY turn boundary to RUN START only — the
# Automation.RunWorker "already-queued half" lesson reversed: a tenant cancel (or, in A2,
# an operator kill) landing between turn N and turn N+1 is silently ignored and the run
# keeps burning turns/budget to its own conclusion. Flips the named cancel red test (a
# cancel issued DURING turn 2 must stop turn 3); its positive control (the same script
# WITHOUT the cancel running turn 3 to the final answer) stays green — proving the red
# fails because the per-turn re-check is gone, not because the loop died.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_loop_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a cancel issued DURING turn 2 stops turn 3
